# CPOS Business Rules

Before implementing features, fixing bugs, or answering product questions about CPOS V2, read and follow:

**`docs/00-business-rules.md`**

That file is the single source of truth for CornerPockets Operating System (CPOS). If any implementation conflicts with it, the document takes precedence.

Key constraints to remember:

- The cashier makes every business decision; CPOS records and calculates.
- Prefer simplicity over cleverness; the cashier should never stop and think.
- Everything belongs to exactly one Business Day (opened and closed manually).
- Counter is today's notebook only — Frames, Cafe, payments, assignment, split. No Outstanding collection, reports, or history.
- Frames support Split (per-contributor Amount / Received / Payment Mode / Due). Cafe does not.
- Due is always calculated (`Amount − Received`), never stored.
- No FIFO, allocation, settlement engine, or hidden payment logic.
- Payment mode: Unassigned when Received = 0; Cash/GPay mandatory when Received > 0.
- Outstanding is created only on Business Day close; cashier collects total Outstanding, never individual records.
- Business Day History is read-only and shows exactly what happened that day.
- Customer page owns Outstanding, Balance History, and customer info — never edits Frames or Cafe Orders.
- If two screens display the same financial metric, they must never calculate it independently. They must consume the same shared aggregation service (`src/lib/financial-summary`).
- Business Day Close is the financial boundary. After close, all financial screens must consume the same finalized financial summaries — no independent aggregation of finalized data.
- Financial Summary Principle: OPEN day may use temporary operational calculations; CLOSED day financial views must derive Bill / Received / Due / Cash / GPay / Outstanding only from shared Financial Summary calculations.
- At Close, persist an immutable Business Day Final Summary (`BusinessDayFinalSummary`). Post-close screens read that record for financial totals — never re-aggregate operational collections for finalized money.
- Game prices live in `src/lib/constants/counter-rates.ts`. Extra Player is never auto-added; staff enter it manually when needed. Stored amounts on historical entries must not change when the rate card updates.

When in doubt, check `docs/00-business-rules.md` before coding.
